 ```
 
+#### Retry
+
+An HTTPRoute rule can retry failed requests with the `retry` field ([GEP-1731](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/geps/gep-1731/)).
+Traefik adds a [Retry middleware](../http/middlewares/retry.md) to the routers created for the rule, after the middlewares of the rule filters:
+
+| Field | Traefik behavior |
+|-------|------------------|
+| `attempts` | Sets the number of retries after the first request. The default is `1`. `0` disables retries. |
+| `codes` | Sets the response status codes that make Traefik retry the request. Traefik does not retry `POST`, `PATCH` and `LOCK` requests on these codes. |
+| `backoff` | Sets the `initialInterval` of the Retry middleware. If not set, Traefik retries immediately. |
+
+Traefik also retries when it cannot connect to the backend.
+
+To retry on `codes`, Traefik keeps the request body in memory, up to the [`retryMaxRequestBodyBytes`](../../install-configuration/providers/kubernetes/kubernetes-gateway.md#opt-providers-kubernetesGateway-retryMaxRequestBodyBytes) provider option.
+A request with a larger body is forwarded without retry on `codes`.
+
+```yaml
+---
+apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
+kind: HTTPRoute
+metadata:
+  name: whoami
+  namespace: default
+spec:
+  parentRefs:
+    - name: traefik
+      sectionName: http
+      kind: Gateway
+
+  hostnames:
+    - whoami.localhost
+
+  rules:
+    - retry:
+        attempts: 2
+        codes:
+          - 502
+          - 503
+        backoff: 100ms
+      backendRefs:
+        - name: whoami
+          namespace: default
+          port: 80
+```
+
 ### GRPC
 
 The `GRPCRoute` is an extended resource in the Gateway API specification, designed to define how GRPC traffic should be routed within a Kubernetes cluster. 
